---
import NowFutureCompare from "./NowFutureCompare.astro";
---

<figure class="viz viz--hh-sheet" data-viz="household-balance-sheet" id="balance-sheet">
  <figcaption class="viz__cap">
    <span class="viz__family">Household Balance Sheet</span>
    <span class="viz__q">Assets − Liabilities = Household Net Wealth</span>
  </figcaption>
  <div class="hh-sheet">
    <div class="hh-sheet__col">
      <h3>Resources</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Earned income</li>
        <li>Benefits</li>
        <li>Ownership / investment income</li>
        <li>Transfers (where applicable)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="hh-sheet__col">
      <h3>Essentials + obligations</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Housing · food · healthcare</li>
        <li>Energy · transportation · care</li>
        <li>Taxes · debt · required payments</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="hh-sheet__col hh-sheet__col--result">
      <h3>Result</h3>
      <p><strong>Prosperity Surplus</strong></p>
      <p class="muted">then balance sheet</p>
      <p><strong>Assets − Liabilities = Net Wealth</strong></p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0.5rem;">
        AR homeownership 66.2% (2022 ACS FACT). AR wealth balances UNKNOWN — US SCF labeled
        NATIONAL_PROXY only.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <NowFutureCompare
    nowLabel="Arkansas household NOW"
    futureLabel="CC household architecture"
    nowText="Wage-dominant resources; high unavoidable costs; thin ownership income; surplus often near zero; time compressed by commute and unpaid care."
    futureText="Broader participation income; controlled essential costs; ownership stakes; usable surplus ladder; discretionary time treated as prosperity — no fake dollar claims."
  />
  <p class="viz__note">
    Thesis test: Constitutional Capitalism succeeds only if households retain more usable surplus,
    greater security, greater ownership, and more discretionary time over time.
  </p>
</figure>
